<title>UK: OKB sets 1.0 billion Czech crown two-year bond.</title>
<headline>OKB sets 1.0 billion Czech crown two-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Creditanstalt Bankverein.</p>
<p> BORROWER   OESTERREICHISCHE KONTROLBANK</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  AUSTRIA</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN CZK   COUPON     10.625    MATURITY    23.DEC.98</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.12    PAY DATE    23.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.25	REOFFER  * 100	 SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES    * RECOMMENDED REOFFER PRICE</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 25-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK/AT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  AUSTRIA   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.00	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EUROSHELF PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
